&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Why At Dotmatics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Dotmatics, a Siemens company,&amp;nbsp; we believe science, data, and decision-making must be deeply intertwined for innovation to thrive. Our Portfolio includes Luma, LumaLab Connect, ELN Platform, Graphpad Prism, Geneious, SnapGene, Protein Metrics, OMIQ, FCS Express, LabArchives, NQuery, EasyPanel, SoftGenetics and Virscidian.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We have a vision for a new Lab of the Future that will change the future of scientific research.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have created the world’s most comprehensive digital science platform – best-of-breed software applications already used by more than 2 million scientists, together in a single ecosystem united by a powerful, flexible enterprise data platform. This is not flat data buried away in digital graveyards. This is dynamic, multi-dimensional decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scientific enterprises need a new level of effectiveness to achieve tomorrow’s breakthroughs. Illness will not wait. The biosphere will not wait. We are tireless in our vision, because the time for innovation is now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shaping the Future of Science At Dotmatics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our global team of more than 800 colleagues are dedicated to supporting our customers in over 180 countries. Together, with our scientific community of users, we accelerate scientific innovation in order to make the world a healthier, cleaner, and safer place to live.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a collaborative, global team pushing the boundaries of scientific innovation.&amp;nbsp; Your ideas and efforts will have a tangible impact, accelerating scientific progress and discovery. We offer a dynamic, remote-friendly environment that fosters high integrity and collaboration, empowering you to excel. Dotmatics is a company built by scientists, for scientists. Combined, we are now the world’s largest cloud-based scientific research R&amp;amp;D platform. We need your help to keep growing and pioneering the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are Science Driven. We are Customer Centric. We are Better Together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dotmatics is seeking a DevOps Engineer to join our team working on ground-breaking Scientific Software products such as Luma.&amp;nbsp; In this role, you will have the opportunity to apply your knowledge to help improve our processes, infrastructure and security by applying best practices with the latest technologies. You will be AI fluent and know how AI influences engineering and DevOps&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will get to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and manage CI/CD and deployment pipelines for both AWS-native and Kubernetes-based applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide advice/assistance to the product teams, clarifying requirements for deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product teams on cloud and container best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage IT infrastructure in cloud computing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation: Use CI tools to automate code changes, builds, testing, and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring: Monitor performance after release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and improve monitoring systems for automated alerts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy: Design and manage the DevOps infrastructure, pipelines, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SECURITY: Embed security into every stage of the delivery lifecycle (DevSecOps), including automated SAST, DAST, dependency, secrets, and container image scanning in CI/CD pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SECURITY: Implement and enforce least-privilege IAM, network segmentation, encryption in transit and at rest, and secrets management (e.g. AWS Secrets Manager, Vault, KMS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SECURITY: Harden Kubernetes clusters and cloud environments using policy-as-code, admission controls, runtime protection, and CIS/NIST benchmarks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SECURITY: Support vulnerability management, incident response, audit readiness, and compliance efforts (e.g. SOC 2, ISO 27001)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI: Use AI-assisted tooling to accelerate pipeline development, infrastructure code, troubleshooting, and incident analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI: Apply AI/ML-driven capabilities to monitoring, including anomaly detection, alert noise reduction, and automated root-cause analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI: Build and operate deployment pipelines and infrastructure for AI/ML and LLM-based workloads, including model serving, GPU-enabled clusters, and cost controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI: Establish guardrails for responsible AI use in engineering workflows, including data privacy, access controls, and review of AI-generated code and configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are looking for people &lt;/strong&gt;who have 8+ years of experience maintaining high-traffic applications and complex technical infrastructure. You will be someone with a proven background in supporting cloud environments, with hands-on experience translating AWS Well-Architected principles into action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The key skills we are looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes clusters/customer cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS (ECS, EKS, ALB, EC2, S3, RDS, CloudFront, Route53, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, CloudFormation, Pulumi)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD tools (Octopus Deploy, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, TeamCity, CodePipeline, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APMs and logging (e.g. Datadog, Grafana, Prometheus, Loki, ELK, App Insights)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Networking concepts in cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software development lifecycle processes/version control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security: DevSecOps practices, AWS security services (IAM, GuardDuty, Security Hub, WAF, Config, KMS), container and supply chain security (image signing, SBOMs), and security scanning tools (e.g. Trivy, Snyk, SonarQube, Checkov)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security: Familiarity with Kubernetes security (RBAC, network policies, Pod Security Standards, OPA/Kyverno) and secrets management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI: Practical experience using AI coding and operations assistants (e.g. GitHub Copilot, Claude, Amazon Q) to improve engineering productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI: Understanding of how to deploy and operate AI/ML workloads (e.g. Amazon Bedrock, SageMaker, model-serving on Kubernetes) and observe their performance and cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI: Awareness of AI-specific risks such as prompt injection, data leakage, and insecure AI-generated code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting languages (e.g. Python, Bash)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux administration and networking (e.g. HTTP/2)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Microservice and serverless architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GitOps tooling (e.g. Argo CD, Flux)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal tooling or agents that apply AI to DevOps workflows (e.g. automated incident triage, ChatOps)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications (e.g. AWS Certified DevOps Engineer, AWS Security Specialty, CKA/CKS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databases (e.g. PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to AI-enabled tooling or workflows, with openness to incorporating AI into day-to-day work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Research shows us the&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2014/05/the-confidence-gap/359815/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2014/05/the-confidence-gap/359815/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;confidence gap&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;imposter syndrome can get in the way of meeting outstanding candidates, so please don’t hesitate to apply — we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree that Dotmatics may collect your personal data for recruiting, global organization planning, and related purposes. Dotmatics &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.dotmatics.com/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://legal.hubspot.com/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; explains what personal information we may process, where we may process your personal information, our purposes for processing your personal information, and the rights you can exercise over Dotmatics use of your personal information.&lt;span class=&quot;c-message__edited_label&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dotmatics is an equal opportunity employer. We are a welcoming place for everyone, and we do our best to make sure all people feel supported and connected at work.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;🚀 We’re on a mission to make money work for everyone.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re waving goodbye to the complicated and confusing ways of traditional banking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After starting as a prepaid card, our product offering has grown a lot in the last 10 years in the UK. As well as&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/personal&quot;&gt;personal&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/business-banking&quot;&gt;business&lt;/a&gt; bank accounts, we offer &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/joint-account&quot;&gt;joint accounts&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/16-17&quot;&gt;accounts for 16-17 year olds&lt;/a&gt;, a &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/under-16s&quot;&gt;free kids account&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/flex&quot;&gt;credit cards&lt;/a&gt; in the UK, with more exciting things to come beyond. Our UK customers can also &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/savings&quot;&gt;save&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/investments&quot;&gt;invest &lt;/a&gt;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/pensions&quot;&gt;combine their pensions&lt;/a&gt; with us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With our hot coral cards and get-paid-early feature, combined with financial education on social media and our award winning customer service, we have a long history of creating magical moments for our customers!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re not about selling products - we want to solve problems and change lives through Monzo ❤️&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;📍London / UK Remote | 💰£142,000 - £170,000 + &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers/&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; ✨&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Financial Control team ⭐&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced finance operations leader for a 12-month fixed-term contract to lead our Global Financial Operations and Control team. The incumbent Director is stepping out of day-to-day operations to spearhead a strategic, multi-year finance automation and systems program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mandate is&amp;nbsp; to provide steady-state operational leadership across all financial operations, close cycles, and management reporting; and serve as the essential operational contact for the program.&amp;nbsp; You will ensure BAU integrity while actively operationalising and absorbing newly automated processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔑 You’ll play a key role by...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading all aspects of financial control and operations, including Accounts Payable, Treasury Operations/Product Control, Money Operations ensuring robust, well controlled, and timely transaction processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the production and end-to-end delivery of monthly close and management reporting cycle, working across Finance to provide the Group Financial Controller, UK CFO and EU CFOs with actionable insights and variance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining a robust, control and governance framework focused on integrity of our data and processes.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serving as the primary operational counterpart and sounding board to the Director of Financial Operations &amp;amp; Control (incumbent) within the programme, providing operational feedback on target operating models and workflow designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing team capacity and workflows to free up key subject matter experts for involvement in the programme, including (not limited to) User Acceptance Testing, parallel runs, and systems testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the practical change management and operational rollout of new automation tools within the live environment, establishing new standard operating procedures without interrupting daily processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with the Director of Financial &amp;amp; Regulatory Reporting to ensure core financial operations and control processes comply with overarching accounting policies&amp;nbsp; and provide a seamless hand off into the consolidation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing stable, empathetic, and accountable leadership to a distributed team during a period of change, maintaining high engagement, retention, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and maintaining effective working relationships with internal stakeholders, external auditors and advisors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving the delivery of the Financial Operations and Control teams milestones and actions on existing key projects such as EU expansion, working with stakeholders to identify and resolve delivery risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing a structured, documented operational handover back to permanent leadership at the conclusion of the 12-month term.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Scope Clarification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Included:&lt;/strong&gt; Global financial operations and control process ownership, including delivery of those services to subsidiaries, Treasury operations/Product control, Money Operations, Month-end Close and related management reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excluded:&lt;/strong&gt; Group Consolidation and the preparation/filing of Statutory Financial Statements for the Group and subsidiaries; Regulatory Reporting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤩 We’d love to hear from you if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a demonstrated track record stepping into high volume, multi-entity finance operations leadership roles and delivering immediate stability within regulated environments (Fintech, Banking, or Financial Services preferred).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an empathetic, effective people leader with a strong track record of coaching individuals and fostering a positive, high-performing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a deep understanding of internal control environments and the ability to build &quot;best-in-class&quot; processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience operating within complex, multi-entity or cross-border structures where data consistency is paramount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have demonstrated experience operationalising new technology, and embedding change within Finance teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have excellent stakeholder management skills, with the ability to explain operational complexities to key stakeholders and peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are adaptability and resilience in fast-paced, tech-led, and agile environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You hold strong technical accounting knowledge (IFRS)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not ticking every box? That’s totally okay! Studies show that women and people of colour might hesitate to apply unless they meet every single requirement. At Monzo, we’re dedicated to creating a diverse and welcoming team. If you’re passionate about this role and keen to learn and grow with us, we encourage you to apply— even if you don’t have everything that&#39;s listed just yet. Drop us your application, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🙌 What’s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 £142,000 - £170,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📍This role can be based in our London office, but we&#39;re open to distributed working within the UK (with ad hoc meetings in London) &lt;strong&gt;*(delete if doesn’t apply)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⏰ We offer flexible working hours and trust you to work enough hours to do your job well, and at times that suit you and your team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 £1,000 learning budget each year to use on books, training courses and conferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏡 We will set you up to work from home; all employees are given Macbooks and for fully remote workers we will provide extra support for your work-from-home setup.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;➕ Plus lots more! &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers/&quot;&gt;Read our full list of benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌈&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; The application journey has 5 key steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initial Call with the Recruiter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring Manager Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Role Specific Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Behavioural Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final Interview with the Team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This process should take around 3-4 weeks - your schedule is really important to us, so we promise to be as flexible as possible!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have some guidelines on using Artificial Intelligence (AI) to ace an application and interview at Monzo.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/the-ultimate-guide-on-using-ai-to-ace-an-interview-at-monzo&quot;&gt;You can read them here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’d prefer to work part-time, please let us know and we&#39;ll make this happen if we can.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;#LI-TP1 #LI-REMOTE&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunities for everyone&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity and inclusion are a priority for us and we’re making sure we have lots of support for all of our people to grow at Monzo. At Monzo, we’re embracing diversity by fostering an inclusive environment for all people to do the best work of their lives with us. This is integral to our mission of making money work for everyone. You can read more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/diversity-and-inclusion&quot;&gt;blog&lt;/a&gt;, 2026 &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/our-2026-diversity-and-inclusion-report&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Diversity and Inclusion Report&lt;/a&gt; and 2025 &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/gender-pay-gap-report-2025&quot;&gt;Gender Pay Gap Report.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer. All applicants will be considered for employment without attention to age, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, family or parental status, national origin, or veteran, neurodiversity or disability status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a preferred name, please use it to apply. We don&#39;t need full or birth names at application stage 😊&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Company You’ll Join&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Carta is the connected platform and AI-native ecosystem for private capital. Built to replace fragmented tools with a single system of record, Carta brings together the software, services, and legal infrastructure that founders use to manage equity, fund managers use to run administration and reporting, and legal teams use to close transactions. Trusted by 55,000 companies and 1.8M+ equity holders in 160+ countries, and 10,000 funds and SPVs representing $250B+ in assets under management, Carta is transforming how private capital operates. Recognized by Fortune, Forbes, Fast Company, Inc. and Great Places to Work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information about our offices and culture, check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://carta.com/careers/&quot;&gt;Carta careers page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Company You’ll Join&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Carta is a platform that helps people manage equity, build businesses, and invest in the companies of tomorrow. Our mission is to unlock the power of equity ownership for more people in more places.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Carta is trusted by more than 40,000 companies and over two million people in nearly 160 countries to manage cap tables, compensation, and valuations. Carta also supports nearly 7,000 funds and SPVs, and represents nearly $130B in assets under administration. Carta&#39;s tender offer solutions have returned $14B to shareholders in secondary transactions. Today, Carta’s platform manages nearly three trillion dollars in equity globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information about our offices and culture, check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://carta.com/careers/&quot;&gt;Carta careers page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Interested in data privacy? Check out our policies on &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://carta.com/privacy/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Privacy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://carta.com/privacy/candidate/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;CA Candidate Privacy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Problems You’ll Solve&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the success and health of a varied EMEA Book of Business across SMB, Mid-Market and Enterprise customers&amp;nbsp; (~ 600 accounts); developing different strategies aimed to increase engagement while mitigating churn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become a trusted advisor; develop consultative relationships (particularly with the Mid-Market and Enterprise segments) by delivering value, sharing best practices and acting as the voice of customers internally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools to scale personalised customer engagement, accelerate EBR and renewal prep, and surface insights across a large book of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product adoption and usage of Carta throughout the customer journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage technology to proactively engage with customers at scale regarding Carta’s values and upcoming renewals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure your customers are getting the most out of Carta Europe’s service offerings, market knowledge and expertise to further enhance their experience as our European customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Team You’ll Work With&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be joining the small but mighty Customer Success team in London in&amp;nbsp; the Carta Europe business unit. The team is looking for a well-rounded, experienced and adaptable Customer Success Manager who’s ready to roll up their sleeves and help drive retention.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This means working closely with not only your fellow UK Customer Success team mates, but many other internal teams from Sales and Delivery teams to RevOps and R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This unique role requires you to be a self-starter, be eager to make your mark, thrive in collaborative teamwork and work dynamically in a fast-paced startup environment. You need to obsess over customer experience and adopting top tier CS practices, alongside unparalleled organisation and communication skills. In addition, we’re prioritising:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in Customer Success or Account Management, preferably in a SaaS environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Salesforce (SFDC) and the ability to quickly learn new systems and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with customer success platforms such as Catalyst, Gainsight, Totango, Vitally, Client Success, or ChurnZero&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable leveraging AI tools, particularly Claude, to accelerate research, synthesize information, and streamline complex workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to navigate difficult conversations while preserving strong customer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset with a proactive approach and bias for action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, listening, facilitation, and negotiation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work autonomously on projects and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data analysis, time management, organizational, and prioritization skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Footer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to providing a positive interview experience for every candidate. If accommodations due to a disability or medical condition are needed, please notify the recruiter via email. As a company, we value fairness, helpfulness, transparency, leadership and build our teams around these values. Check out our&lt;a href=&quot;https://carta.com/careers/&quot;&gt; careers page&lt;/a&gt; to get to know us better as you think about your next step at Carta.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important Security Notice for Candidates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our company has been targeted by individuals creating fake domains similar to ours to scam prospects and candidates. Please note that all official communications from us will come from ----- Be cautious of any requests for sensitive information or payments outside of our official channels. For more information about this type of scam, please review &lt;a href=&quot;https://consumer.ftc.gov/consumer-alerts/2023/08/scammers-impersonate-well-known-companies-recruit-fake-jobs-linkedin-and-other-job-platforms&quot;&gt;the guidelines &lt;/a&gt;provided by the Federal Trade Commission (FTC). If you encounter any suspicious activity, please report it immediately to &lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;​​Awards and Acknowledgements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Companies and funds like Tribe and Pipe build their businesses on Carta. The company has been included on the&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.forbes.com/lists/cloud100/?sh=2b8dd7e27d9c&quot;&gt; Forbes World’s Best Cloud Companies&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fastcompany.com/most-innovative-companies/2020&quot;&gt; Fast Company&#39;s Most Innovative&lt;/a&gt; list, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.inc.com/inc5000/2020&quot;&gt; Inc.’s Fastest-Growing Private Companies&lt;/a&gt;. We’ve also been recognized as a&lt;a href=&quot;https://builtin.com/awards/us/2023/best-places-to-work&quot;&gt; 2023 Built In Best Place to Work in the U.S.&lt;/a&gt;, a&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.themuse.com/advice/vibe-awards-2022-vacation-time-off-benefits&quot;&gt; Muse VIBE Award winner in the Vacation and Time Off category&lt;/a&gt; and certified as a&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greatplacetowork.com/certified-company/7036977&quot;&gt; Great Place to Work&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Interested in our candidate privacy policy? Find out more&lt;a href=&quot;https://carta.com/privacy/candidate/&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Disclosures:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to providing a positive interview experience for every candidate. If accommodations due to a disability or medical condition are needed, please connect with the talent partner via email.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carta uses E-Verify in the United States for employment authorization. See the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/about-e-verify/what-is-e-verify&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;Department&quot;&gt;Department of Justice&lt;/a&gt; websites for more details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For information on our data privacy policies, see&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://carta.com/privacy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://carta.com/privacy/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Privacy&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://carta.com/privacy/candidate/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://carta.com/privacy/candidate/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;CA Candidate Privacy&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://carta.com/legal/br/brazil-pay-transparency/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://carta.com/legal/br/brazil-pay-transparency/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Brazil Transparency Report&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note that all official communications from us will come from an ----- or ----- domain. Report any contact from unapproved domains to -----
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Customer Success Manager, you will proactively drive new product attachment and effective strong relationships across our largest and most strategic customers. You’ll advocate for the customer internally and focus on a positive customer experience. Interactions are rooted in relationship-management, first and foremost, while also advocating for growth opportunities. Enterprise Customer Success Managers follow a well-defined methodology that helps them identify the customer&#39;s unique needs and clearly convey the value of the Datadog product.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic partner to customers, orchestrating cross-functional internal teams and engaging executive, technical, and business stakeholders to understand customer goals and translate them into a clear, deliverable Datadog value narrative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively build and maintain executive relationships to deliver clear, outcome-driven value stories that connect Datadog technical use cases to measurable business results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead QBRs and strategic reviews as a forum to demonstrate impact, align on priorities, and define next-step initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze adoption and usage trends to quantify value delivered, extract insights from large datasets, identify gaps, and drive financially grounded commercial recommendations and strategic opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position Datadog as a critical observability platform that enables reliability, efficiency, and informed decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and project manage the on-boarding process for new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with AEs, SEs, TAM, Product, Support, Enablement and other technical teams to ensure consistent value delivery and messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With demonstrated understanding of observability and security platforms, align customers technical and business objectives to our platform offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-centric with 3+ years in a Customer Success or Account Management role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to manage a wide portfolio of accounts rolling up to large enterprise corporate accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledgeable in working with Fortune 1000 companies and global brands across all industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong communicator with exceptional attention to detail and an ability to cater to a specific audience, including CTO, VP of Engineering and DevOps professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in the B2B tech space or with SaaS companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel for customer onsite visits and events as required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in written and spoken English and German&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Growth:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-breed onboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous global benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intra-departmental mentor and buddy program for in-house networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New hire stock equity (RSUs) and employee stock purchase plan (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous professional development, product training, and career pathing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inclusive company culture, able to join our Community Guilds and Inclusion Talks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits and Growth listed above may vary based on the country of your employment and the nature of your employment with Datadog.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Datadog:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog is the leading observability and security platform for the AI era, providing businesses with unified visibility across the technology stack to manage complexity at scale. It brings applications, infrastructure, data, models, and security into one place, using AI to detect and resolve issues before they impact customers. Trusted globally by Fortune 500 companies and high-growth AI leaders, Datadog enables businesses to move faster with clarity and confidence. Learn more about #DatadogLife on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/datadoghq/?hl=en&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/datadog&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn,&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://learn.datadoghq.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Datadog Learning Center. &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;215&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunity at Datadog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog is proud to offer &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;equal employment opportunity&lt;/a&gt; to everyone regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, veteran status, and other characteristics protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements. Here are our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/candidate-legal-notices/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Legal Notices&lt;/a&gt; for your reference.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog endeavors to make our Careers Page accessible to all users. If you would like to contact us regarding the accessibility of our website or need assistance completing the application process, please complete &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeoJeduEZ2NdZF_65uZmWUrCM-zee7yADXX1s6Xr9zAGq8iKA/viewform&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;this form&lt;/a&gt;. This form is for accommodation requests only and cannot be used to inquire about the status of applications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Privacy and AI Guidelines:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;Any information you submit to Datadog as part of your application will be processed in accordance with Datadog’s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. For information on our AI policy, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/interviewing-at-datadog-ai-guidelines/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Interviewing at Datadog AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-family: &#39;Instrument Sans&#39;, &#39;Segoe UI&#39;, Trebuchet MS, Tahoma, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Vast is developing next-generation space stations and space infrastructure using an incremental, hardware-rich, and capital-efficient approach. Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station to support a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and supporting a growing space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to design, build, and operate its own spacecraft in orbit. Next, Haven-1 is targeted to become the world’s first commercial space station, with launch anticipated in 2027, followed by additional Haven modules. Additionally, the company recently announced two new offerings leveraging its space station components and the heritage of Haven Demo: Vast Satellite, a high-power satellite product line; and Vast Lunar Systems, power, communications, and habitats for the Moon.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in Long Beach, California, and with more than 1,000 employees and over a billion dollars in private capital, Vast has built the facilities capable of manufacturing America’s next space station. The company plans to develop future habitats and systems for Mars, dedicated modules for government partners, and other crewed systems designed to unlock the expanding long-term space economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast recherche un(e) &lt;strong&gt;Directeur(trice), Développement Commercial International - Satellites&lt;/strong&gt;, sous la responsabilité du &lt;strong&gt;SVP, Satellite Business Development &amp;amp; Commercialization&lt;/strong&gt;, pour diriger le développement commercial axé sur le commerce (communications, observation de la Terre, détection, défense et applications de calcul en orbite) et les gouvernements internationaux pour Vast Satellites. Ce rôle est centré sur les marchés hors États-Unis — notamment l&#39;Europe, le Moyen-Orient et l&#39;Asie — et dirigera l&#39;engagement client, le développement des opportunités, la stratégie de capture, l&#39;engagement gouvernemental/défense et les efforts de partenariat qui font progresser les initiatives de Vast pour développer, fabriquer et exploiter des plateformes de bus satellites avancées.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Il s&#39;agit d&#39;une petite équipe commerciale fondatrice de haut niveau : le rôle exige à la fois des instincts de « hunter » en développement commercial (créer des marchés et de la demande là où il n&#39;en existe pas encore) et des compétences avérées de « closer » (négocier et exécuter des contrats allant de quelques millions à des centaines de millions de dollars).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ce poste sera à &lt;strong&gt;temps plein, exempté&lt;/strong&gt;, ouvert à un lieu de travail international flexible comme décrit ci-dessus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsabilités :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Élaborer et exécuter une stratégie globale de marché commercial et gouvernemental international couvrant l&#39;Europe, le Moyen-Orient et l&#39;Asie, alignée sur les objectifs commerciaux de Vast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Établir et maintenir une veille stratégique sur le marché et la concurrence concernant les clients spatiaux commerciaux et gouvernementaux internationaux, en distinguant le positionnement de Vast de celui de ses concurrents dans chaque région.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter la planification interne pour la priorisation des opportunités internationales, la stratégie de capture et le développement du pipeline sur de multiples marchés alliés et partenaires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diriger l&#39;engagement client à travers l&#39;identification d&#39;opportunités, la définition du périmètre des missions, les présentations de capacités et le développement de concepts précoces avec les opérateurs commerciaux internationaux, les sociétés d&#39;observation de la Terre, les ministères de la défense et les entités gouvernementales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tirer parti d&#39;un solide réseau préexistant de haut niveau au sein de la chaîne de valeur internationale de l&#39;espace et de la défense pour ouvrir des portes auprès de clients potentiels et identifier précocement les menaces concurrentielles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diriger l&#39;élaboration des propositions et coordonner les contributions interfonctionnelles des équipes d&#39;ingénierie, de gestion de programme, de finance, juridique et de contrôle des exportations/conformité, avec le soutien de l&#39;analyste BD et de l&#39;ingénieur avant-vente de l&#39;équipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assumer la responsabilité du développement du pipeline, des prévisions et des rapports pour tous les comptes commerciaux et gouvernementaux internationaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Négocier et conclure des contrats pour des missions commerciales et gouvernementales/défense internationales et les services associés, en naviguant à travers divers cadres nationaux de passation de marchés, de contrôle des exportations (ex. ITAR/EAR) et de partenariat.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Se coordonner avec l&#39;équipe de sécurité nationale de Vast lorsque les programmes internationaux croisent des parties prenantes ou des enjeux liés au gouvernement américain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Représenter Vast lors d&#39;événements de l&#39;industrie spatiale, aérospatiale et de défense internationale en Europe, au Moyen-Orient et en Asie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Faire des présentations, participer à des panels et fournir des briefings de haut niveau/C-suite communiquant les capacités et la valeur des plateformes satellites de Vast aux audiences commerciales, gouvernementales et de défense internationales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications Minimales :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus de 12 ans d&#39;expérience pertinente dans le développement commercial spatial/aérospatial, les ventes, la gestion de capture ou les contrats gouvernementaux/défense, avec un succès avéré en Europe, au Moyen-Orient et/ou en Asie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Historique avéré d&#39;origination et de conclusion personnelle de contrats, y compris des transactions de plusieurs dizaines de millions de dollars ou plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relations établies et vérifiables avec des clients potentiels au niveau cadre et exécutif, et connaissance du paysage concurrentiel sur de multiples marchés spatiaux et de défense internationaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience dans la chaîne de valeur spatiale/aérospatiale (lancement, bus satellite, charge utile, intégration maître d&#39;œuvre ou opérations), idéalement complémentaire des opérations satellites — par ex. observation de la Terre ou défense internationale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compréhension approfondie des structures de passation de marchés et de partenariat gouvernementales internationales pertinentes pour les programmes d&#39;espace et de défense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solides compétences techniques et capacité à communiquer des systèmes complexes à des audiences commerciales, de défense et gouvernementales internationales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellentes capacités de communication, d&#39;analyse, de collaboration et de relations interpersonnelles ; à l&#39;aise pour opérer à travers diverses cultures et langues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à opérer de manière autonome, à hiérarchiser les priorités efficacement et à gérer simultanément plusieurs projets internationaux dans un environnement de petite équipe au rythme soutenu.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compétences et Expériences Souhaitées :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relations et crédibilité établies en Europe, au Moyen-Orient et en Asie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise des langues pertinentes pour les marchés cibles (français, arabe, japonais, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience de travail aux côtés d&#39;équipes d&#39;affaires publiques locales ou coordination avec celles-ci (ex. affaires publiques gouvernementales françaises/UE).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connaissance des régimes de contrôle des exportations (ITAR/EAR) dans les programmes de satellites internationaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exigences Supplémentaires :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à voyager plus de 50 % du temps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Director, Satellite Business Development International&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;SVP, Satellite Business Development &amp;amp; Commercialization&lt;/strong&gt;, to lead commercial (communications, Earth observation, sensing, defense, and in-orbit compute applications) and international government-focused business development for Vast Satellites. This role is focused on markets outside the United States — including Europe, the Middle East, and Asia — and will lead customer engagement, opportunity development, capture strategy, government/defense engagement, and partnership efforts that advance Vast&#39;s initiatives to develop, manufacture, and operate advanced satellite bus platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a small, senior founding commercial team: the role demands both business development &quot;hunter&quot; instincts (creating markets and demand where none exist yet) and proven &quot;closer&quot; skills (negotiating and executing contracts from single-digit millions to hundreds of millions of dollars).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time, exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position open to a flexible international location as described above.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a comprehensive international commercial and government market strategy spanning Europe, the Middle East, and Asia, aligned with Vast&#39;s business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a market and competitive intelligence view across international commercial and government space customers, distinguishing Vast&#39;s positioning from competitors in each region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead internal planning for international opportunity prioritization, capture strategy, and pipeline development across multiple allied and partner markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer engagement across opportunity identification, mission scoping, capability briefings, and early concept development with international commercial operators, Earth observation companies, defense ministries, and government entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage a strong, pre-existing senior-level network across the international space/defense value chain to open doors with potential customers and identify competitive threats early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead proposal development and coordinate cross-functional contributions from engineering, program management, finance, legal, and export-control/compliance teams, supported by the team&#39;s BD analyst and pre-sales engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own pipeline development, forecasting, and reporting across all international commercial and government accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and close contracts for international commercial and government/defense missions and associated services, navigating varying national procurement, export-control (e.g., ITAR/EAR), and partnership frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Vast&#39;s National Security team where international programs intersect with US Government stakeholders or content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Vast at international space, aerospace, and defense industry events across Europe, the Middle East, and Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver presentations, participate in panels, and provide senior/C-suite-level briefings that communicate the capabilities and value of Vast&#39;s satellite platforms to international commercial, government, and defense audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of relevant experience in space/aerospace business development, sales, capture management, or government/defense contracting, with demonstrated success operating in Europe, the Middle East, and/or Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of personally originating and closing contracts, including deals in the tens of millions of dollars or above.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established, verifiable senior and executive-level relationships with potential customers, and knowledge of the competitive landscape across multiple international space/defense markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in the space/aerospace value chain (launch, satellite bus, payload, prime integration, or operations), ideally complementary to satellite operations — e.g., Earth observation or international defense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of international government procurement and partnership structures relevant to space and defense programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical understanding and ability to communicate complex systems to international commercial, defense, and government audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, analytical, collaboration, and interpersonal skills; comfortable operating across cultures and languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, prioritize effectively, and manage multiple international efforts simultaneously in a fast-paced, lean-team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships and credibility across Europe, the Middle East, and Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in languages relevant to target markets (French, Arabic, Japanese, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working alongside or coordinating with in-country government affairs teams (e.g., French/EU government affairs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with export-control regimes (ITAR/EAR) in international satellite programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel 50%+ of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-family: &#39;Instrument Sans&#39;, &#39;Segoe UI&#39;, Trebuchet MS, Tahoma, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We calibrate level and compensation to the selected candidate&#39;s experience and demonstrated capability. We welcome applicants across a range of experience levels to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EQUAL OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Vast is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with Vast is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Durée :&lt;/strong&gt; 6 mois – Temps plein&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Période :&lt;/strong&gt; à partir de mars 2026&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Localisation :&lt;/strong&gt; Paris 9e&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Encadré par :&lt;/strong&gt; la responsable communication de l’événement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;À propos d’Artefact Open Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Artefact Open Innovation, nous sommes des entrepreneurs convaincus que la compétitivité, l’efficacité et la transformation des grandes organisations se gagnent en développant de nouvelles formes de collaborations et une compréhension des enjeux liés à l’adoption des nouvelles technologies – notamment DATA et IA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pour cela, nous partageons et propageons l’esprit entrepreneur avec des modes de collaboration plus agiles à l’échelle :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Des individus&lt;/strong&gt;, à travers des programmes de formation et l’accélération de projets d’innovation&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Des équipes&lt;/strong&gt;, grâce à des expériences d’innovation participative et l’adoption de nouveaux modes de collaboration&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Des écosystèmes et des organisations&lt;/strong&gt;, en créant et animant de larges communautés ouvertes (open innovation), mobilisées autour d’objectifs communs&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dans ce cadre, nous recherchons un·e &lt;strong&gt;stagiaire communication orienté·e contenus digitaux&lt;/strong&gt;, pour accompagner la chargée de communication au sein du pôle événementiel &amp;amp; communication sur la production et la diffusion des contenus avant, pendant et après l’événement France Quantum et la stratégie autour de l&#39;événement Adopt AI - Grand Palais.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Missions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En soutien direct à la chargée de communication, vous interviendrez sur un large spectre de missions :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Création de contenus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Création de visuels sur Canva&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Montage de courtes vidéos dynamiques pour les réseaux sociaux (reels, stories, teasers, formats événementiels)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rédaction de posts pour valoriser les speakers, partenaires et écosystèmes (recherche, industrie, tech, innovation…)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Déclinaison des contenus selon les temps forts du projet (annonces, teasing, live event, post-event)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programmation et modération des publications sur LinkedIn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Veille et participation à l’animation des communautés&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Suivi des performances des contenus et remontée d’insights&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partenariats &amp;amp; diffusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Suivi des échanges liés aux contreparties partenaires (visibilité, posts, formats dédiés)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Création et envoi de mailings marketing&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-événement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tri et sélection des photos&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rédaction des posts de remerciement et de valorisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vérification et mise en ligne des replays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aide à l’organisation des retours d’expérience (REX)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribution à la réflexion stratégique&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participation aux réflexions autour de la stratégie de contenus et de la ligne éditoriale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brainstorming sur de nouveaux formats de contenus et de nouveaux canaux de communication&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribution à la réflexion sur&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;la mise en place d’un rétroplanning éditorial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;la structuration de packages de communication pour les partenaires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Le ou la stagiaire sera force de proposition et impliqué·e dans la réflexion, les décisions finales relevant de la responsable communication.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profil recherché&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Étudiant·e en Master communication, marketing ou équivalent, avec quelques expériences en stage en communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Créatif·ve, curieux·se, avec un fort attrait pour l’IA et l’événementiel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonne maîtrise de la création de visuels et goût prononcé pour l’image (photo &amp;amp; vidéo)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellente orthographe en français et bilingue anglais (pour suivre et participer à l’écrit &amp;amp; à l’oral dans les deux langues)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organisé·e, rigoureux·se, capable de gérer plusieurs projets en simultané&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonome, dynamique, force de proposition, avec un excellent relationnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;À l’affût des tendances en communication digitale et social media&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compétences techniques&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Canva indispensable, Photoshop est un plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outils de montage vidéo : CapCut, Premiere Rush ou équivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connaissance d’outils de mailing (Pardot ou autre)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conditions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gratification : selon profil et convention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lieu : Paris 9e, avec possibilité de télétravail partiel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chez Artefact, nous recrutons nos collaborateurs uniquement en fonction de nos besoins et des qualités propres de chaque candidat. Nous assurons le développement de leurs compétences professionnelles et de leurs responsabilités sans discrimination d’aucune sorte, notamment de croyances, de genre, d’âge, de situation d&#39;handicap, d’origine ethnique, d’orientation sexuelle, d’appartenance à une organisation politique, religieuse, syndicale ou à une minorité.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

