&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Come join the organization that is redefining security for the AI era. As one of the&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wiz.io/blog/100m-arr-in-18-months-wiz-becomes-the-fastest-growing-software-company-ever&quot;&gt; fastest-growing startups ever,&lt;/a&gt; we enable teams to secure cloud and AI applications by connecting code, cloud, and runtime into a single shared context. Trusted by security teams all over the world, we have a proven&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.g2.com/products/wiz-wiz/reviews&quot;&gt; track record of success&lt;/a&gt; and a culture that values world-class talent. Not to mention, we&#39;re now&lt;a href=&quot;https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/identity-security/google-completes-acquisition-of-wiz&quot;&gt; powered by Google&lt;/a&gt;, meaning we offer our customers an AI-powered platform that harnesses Google’s Threat Intelligence and Security Operations to better detect, prevent, and respond to threats across all environments, allowing for further innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Wizards from all over the globe work together to protect the infrastructure of our customers, including over 65% of the Fortune 100, who trust us to scan and secure over 230 billion files daily. We’re honored to be a leading player in a massive and growing market, and we continue to look for exceptional Wizards who are eager to make a significant impact on our team. At Wiz, you’ll have the freedom to think creatively, dream big, and use your full range of skills to contribute to our momentous growth. Come join our team and help us create secure cloud environments that allow even the best companies to move faster, all while having some fun!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 2 years of experience selling SMB/Mid-Enterprise solutions in the SaaS or security space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining an accurate Salesforce (SFDC) pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to C-level executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of SaaS sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of hitting or exceeding targets year after year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Managed Security Service Providers (MSSPs), specifically regarding &quot;sell-to&quot; and &quot;sell-through&quot; motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security or cloud security domain expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a fast-paced start-up environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good standing relationships with previous sales operation teams, operating with the mindset that selling is a team sport.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process-oriented and detail-oriented operational approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to take a consultative approach to provide professional advice and pivot in meetings based on customer needs rather than sticking to a script.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be reporting to &lt;strong&gt;Josh Averill,&amp;nbsp;Regional Director, Sales&lt;/strong&gt;. This role requires a strong ability to generate pipeline, manage full sales cycles, and articulate the value of security solutions to technical and business stakeholders. You will work alongside a team of &quot;Wizards&quot; that focus on our customer&#39;s business needs. Our priority is building a secure infrastructure for their cloud environments. We do that by learning their business. We ask questions. We listen. We help educate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a secure infrastructure for cloud environments by learning customers&#39; businesses, asking questions, listening, and helping to educate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain operational excellence by being process-oriented and detail-oriented, taking pride in maintaining an accurate SFDC pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain good standing relationships with sales operation teams, collaborating cross-functionally under the belief that selling is a team sport.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a consultative sales approach to provide professional advice and pivot in meetings based on customer needs rather than sticking to a script.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet or exceed sales targets consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell SaaS/Security SMB/Mid-Enterprise solutions directly to C-level executives and manage SaaS sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with MSSPs specifically regarding both &quot;sell-to&quot; and &quot;sell-through&quot; motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate a fast-paced start-up environment with agility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot;&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the country where the position is based,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot;&gt;without the need for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot;&gt;visa &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot;&gt;sponsorship.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot;&gt;This&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot;&gt; role does not offer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot;&gt;visa&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot;&gt;sponsorship&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW149741735 BCX0&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wiz is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you acknowledge that Wiz will process your personal data in accordance with &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wiz.io/legal/privacy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Wiz&#39;s Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager, R&amp;amp;D Quality Assurance independently performs the R&amp;amp;D QA Program Lead role for assigned clinical studies, providing Clinical Quality Assurance oversight in accordance with study protocols, company procedures, GCP requirements, and applicable local and international regulations. The role leads and supports quality oversight, audit, and inspection-readiness activities and works cross-functionally to identify, assess, mitigate, and escalate quality and compliance risks. The Senior Manager also provides guidance and oversight to junior R&amp;amp;D QA staff, as applicable, and supports continuous improvement activities within R&amp;amp;D Quality Assurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role that can be based in Cambridge, MA; Philadelphia, PA; or Maidenhead, UK, with three days per week onsite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently perform the R&amp;amp;D QA Program Lead role for assigned clinical studies, providing Clinical Quality Assurance oversight in accordance with study protocols, company procedures, GCP requirements, and applicable local and international regulations, with escalation to the GCP QA Director as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide quality oversight for assigned clinical studies, including identification, assessment, mitigation, and escalation of quality and compliance risks and support for the investigation and resolution of Quality Events and CAPAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support GCP audit activities, including investigator site, vendor, study, and process audits, as applicable, and ensure audit observations and associated corrective and preventive actions are appropriately addressed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead inspection-readiness activities for assigned clinical studies, including coordination of QA and cross-functional activities, identification and mitigation of potential inspection risks, and preparation for FDA, EMA, PMDA, and other Health Authority inspections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain effective working relationships with internal Alnylam Expertise Area leads, study teams, vendors, and external partners to support study quality, compliance, and inspection-readiness activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain current knowledge of applicable global GCP regulations, regulatory guidance, and industry practices and support continuous improvement of R&amp;amp;D QA processes, procedures, and tools, as applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance, coaching, and oversight to assigned junior R&amp;amp;D QA staff, as applicable, to support effective execution of assigned activities and continued development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree, preferably life science (technology, biological science, pharmacy, or other health related discipline preferred) or equivalent qualification or clinical research experience. Master’s degree in a science, technology, or industry related discipline, preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seven years’ experience in GCP Quality Assurance, or similar experience working in GCP and clinical trial that support pharmaceutical development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in overseeing late phase clinical trials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in leading audits preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting and leading inspections readiness efforts and direct inspection experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience working with different Quality Assurance functions, knowledge of Auditing, Clinical Supply Chain, Clinical Operations, Monitoring, Regulatory Affairs, Clinical Research, Drug Safety, Data Management, Programming and Statistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge &amp;amp; knowledge of how to interpret GCP regulations as well as industry guidance (e.g., FDA, EMA, and other national agencies).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Alnylam: &lt;/strong&gt;Alnylam Pharmaceuticals (Nasdaq: ALNY) has led the translation of RNA interference (RNAi) into a whole new class of innovative medicines with the potential to transform the lives of people afflicted with rare and more prevalent diseases. Based on Nobel Prize-winning science, RNAi therapeutics represent a powerful, clinically validated approach to treating diseases at their genetic source by “interfering” with mRNA that cause or contribute to disease. Since our founding in 2002, Alnylam has led the RNAi Revolution and continues to turn scientific possibility into reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our culture:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Our people-first culture is guided by our core values: fiercely innovative, open culture, purposeful urgency, passion for excellence, and commitment to people, and these values influence how we work and the business decisions we make. Thanks to feedback from our employees over the years, we’ve been fortunate to be named a top employer around the world. Alnylam is extremely proud to have been recognized as one of Science Magazine’s Top Biopharma Employers, one of America&#39;s Most Responsible Companies for 2024 by Newsweek, a Fast Company Best Workplace for Innovators, and a Great Place to Work in Canada, France, Italy, Spain, Switzerland, and UK – among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alnylam, we commit to an inclusive recruitment process and equal employment opportunity. We are dedicated to building an environment where employees can feel that they belong, can bring their authentic selves to work, and achieve to their full potential. By empowering employees to embrace their unique differences at work, our business grows stronger with advanced and original thinking, allowing us to bring groundbreaking medicines to patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before applying, please review Alnylam&#39;s ⁠Candidate&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://alnylampolicies.com/&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;regarding how Alnylam handles Personal Data you provide with your application for employment.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alnylam Pharmaceuticals is seeking an imaginative physician drug developer. This is an opportunity to provide clinical leadership in developing RNAi therapeutics in Alnylam’s rapidly expanding portfolio, which spans the areas of rare genetic diseases, cardio-metabolic diseases, neuroscience, hematology and hepatology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate’s primary role will be to drive the pipeline forward through leadership of clinical development programs.&amp;nbsp; While the primary focus responsibility will be as clinical lead physician on Alnylam’s Huntington’s program, the role may support across a range of therapeutic areas and all stages of development may be required as pipeline assets evolve. The Executive Director is expected to play a leading and influencing role in the overall clinical development strategies and drive progress and operational excellence for associated clinical trials. In addition, this role will include interaction with Alnylam’s research group, helping to advise the team on the clinical development feasibility of novel targets and the design of proof-of-concept studies. This work will also involve extensive consultation and collaboration with external experts. It is expected that additional opportunities will arise to lead bench-to-bedside early phase clinical development programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Executive Director, Clinical Research, will work in a matrix organization across Regulatory, Biostatistics, Clinical Operations, Preclinical, Commercial &amp;amp; QA teams to ensure fully harmonized and integrated development strategies. They will be a key Alnylam Development spokesperson at external meetings, including regulatory interactions and scientific meetings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is hybrid, requiring weekly onsite presence and will be primarily located at our Cambridge, MA headquarters or Maidenhead, UK location. Relocation may be possible for the selected candidate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the strategic leader providing a strong, clear voice for the clinical programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop creative but realistic approaches to drug development and lead clinical efforts to secure global regulatory approvals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversight of trial conduct and safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic consultation and guidance to Research on all decisions that have significant clinical components and implications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Preclinical, Regulatory Affairs, Medical Affairs and Commercial to ensure tight strategic integration of product development plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable via Clinical Research and Operations for all relevant timelines and deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive/supervise all major written deliverables&amp;nbsp;(regulatory submissions, original articles, abstracts), and presentation materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible (as appropriate in line with SOPs) for final review and sign off with respect to all controlled documents including protocols, IBs, informed consent forms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence internal and external audiences in a high impact, highly visible fashion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MD with strong research background or MD PhD, with a track record of successful research support and peer review publications. Board Certification (or equivalent) or specialist training is highly desirable; drug development experience in neurology (Huntington’s Disease) would be a great advantage, but not essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years industry experience or equivalent clinical academic experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound scientific and clinical judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful track record of leading Phase 2/3 clinical programs (preferably in Huntington’s drug development), including major interactions with Health Authorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with concepts of clinical research and clinical trial design, including biostatistics, regulatory agency organization, guidelines, and practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to effectively present ideas and document complex medical/clinical concepts in both written and oral communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of solving problems while exhibiting superior judgment and a balanced, realistic understanding of issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding leadership and collaboration skills working within a matrix environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and knowledge of working with biotech/pharma partner(s) a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in highly entrepreneurial biotech environment and embraces Alnylam’s culture of science, passion and urgency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-HM1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About THG&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are THG, a global ecommerce group on a mission to be the global online leader in beauty and sports nutrition.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our portfolio of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; leading retailers and brands such as LOOKFANTASTIC, Myprotein, ESPA, Perricone MD, and Cult Beauty form our two core businesses: THG Beauty and THG Nutrition.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;From Manchester to New York, we’re powered by a team of over 2500 people who work together, lead by example, and think BIG.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;With us, you’ll go further, faster. What are you waiting for?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About THG&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are THG, a global ecommerce group on a mission to be the global online leader in beauty and sports nutrition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our leading retailers and brands, including LOOKFANTASTIC, Myprotein, ESPA, Perricone MD and Cult Beauty, make up our two core businesses: THG Beauty and THG Nutrition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From Manchester to New York, we’re powered by a team of over 2500 people who work together, lead by example, and think BIG.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With us, you’ll go further, faster. What are you waiting for?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Icon 1, WA15 0AF &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Technical Programme Manager to lead the delivery of our most important customer-facing technology programmes, reporting directly to the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Chief Technology Officer&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;THG runs several high-profile ecommerce websites in nutrition and beauty, including myprotein.com and lookfantastic.com. Our websites and mobile apps are how customers find, buy and come back to our brands, and the programmes you lead will shape that experience directly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own programmes from first idea to launch, mainly across our websites and mobile apps. Examples include personalisation, loyalty and digital marketing technology, and some programmes will reach into other parts of the technology estate. The role is an even mix of programme and project management. You will run long-lived programmes that span many teams, and drive individual projects hands-on when they need it. You will work with executives to decide what gets built and in what order, and tell them plainly how delivery is going.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don’t need to be the architect. Our technology leaders set the technical direction and you will follow their lead. You do need to understand how large websites and apps are built well enough to plan the work, spot risks early and ask the right questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Technical Programme Manager you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Own the delivery of large technology programmes across our websites and mobile apps, from scoping and planning through to launch and review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme Planning:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build and maintain programme plans, milestones and dependency maps across several engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-On Project Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Run individual projects directly when a programme needs it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prioritisation &amp;amp; Product Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Prioritisation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Bring options, costs and trade-offs to executives and secure a clear decision on what comes first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backlog Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Manage the backlog for your programmes so engineering teams always know what is next and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Work with product managers to turn business goals into well-defined, deliverable pieces of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting, Risk &amp;amp; Vendors&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Honest Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Give executives and stakeholders clear, candid updates on progress, risks and dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk &amp;amp; Dependency Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Find risks, blockers and cross-team dependencies early, resolve them, and escalate when a decision is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Hold external vendors and delivery partners to their commitments and fit their work into our plans and releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ways of Working:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Improve how we plan, track and report on delivery across the technology organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A day in the life&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your day is split between the teams doing the work and the leaders deciding what the work should be. You might start with an engineering team, checking progress against the plan and clearing a blocker, then spend time with a product manager breaking a loyalty feature into deliverable stages. In the afternoon you could review a vendor’s delivery plan for a marketing technology integration, then update programme status ahead of an executive review, where you’ll set out where things stand, what is at risk and which decisions you need. You’ll leave with clear priorities and take them back to the teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What skills and experience do I need for this role?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly Skilled in technical programme or project management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with software engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept at delivering customer-facing websites or mobile apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent at managing programmes across several teams, including planning, dependency management and release coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running prioritisation and backlog management with senior stakeholders and reporting on delivery to executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing both external vendors or delivery partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with websites and ecommerce at large scale: high traffic, many markets, or several brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering programmes in personalisation, loyalty or digital marketing technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering native mobile apps alongside web.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in retail, particularly nutrition or beauty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of bringing clear structure to ambiguous, multi-team programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication, with the ability to explain a complex programme to executives in plain terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THG is proud to be a Disability Confident Committed employer. If you are invited to interview, please let us know if there are any reasonable adjustments we can make to the recruitment process that will enable you to perform to the best of your ability.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THG is committed to creating a diverse &amp;amp; inclusive environment and hence welcomes applications from all sections of the community.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Because of the high volumes of applications our opportunities attract, it sometimes takes us time to review and consider them all. We endeavour to respond to every application we receive within 14 days. If you haven&#39;t heard from us within that time frame or should you have any specific questions about this or other applications for positions at THG please contact one of our &lt;span class=&quot;mark75xs2u5gf&quot; data-markjs=&quot;true&quot; data-ogac=&quot;&quot; data-ogab=&quot;&quot; data-ogsc=&quot;&quot; data-ogsb=&quot;&quot;&gt;Talent&lt;/span&gt; team to discuss further.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ui-provider a b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak&quot;&gt;Newsweek is the global media organization that has earned audience time and trust for more than 90 years. Newsweek reaches 100 million people each month with thought-provoking news, opinion, images, graphics, and video delivered across a dozen print and digital platforms. Headquartered in New York City, Newsweek also publishes international editions in EMEA and Asia.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Commercial Director – Events &amp;amp; Strategic Partnerships&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:120}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Newsweek | UK / International | Full-time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;ROLE OVERVIEW&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Newsweek is seeking an experienced, commercially driven Sales Director to lead front-end revenue generation across our B2B events, sponsored content, special reports and strategic partnership portfolio.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;This is a senior, hands-on new-business role for a consultative seller who can turn market insight, industry trends and client business priorities into high-value commercial partnerships.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The role spans Newsweek&#39;s key international growth sectors: AI &amp;amp; FinTech, Healthcare, Sustainability (including Food &amp;amp; Agri-Tech) and Travel &amp;amp; Tourism. We are looking for a commercially versatile individual who can identify opportunities across different industries, develop compelling propositions and personally convert them into revenue.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The successful candidate will operate at the intersection of sales, research, strategy and content. They will identify commercially relevant sectors and themes, engage senior decision-makers, understand their objectives and build bespoke solutions spanning event sponsorship, thought leadership, sponsored content, executive engagement and related Newsweek platforms.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;This is not a traditional advertising or transactional sponsorship-sales role. We are looking for someone who can originate opportunities, shape the proposition with internal teams and personally lead complex conversations through to close.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;UK-based role with competitive salary and commission. Working hours are normally 9am to 6pm. Attendance at our London Canary Wharf office is required at least twice a week. Occasional overseas travel required.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;KEY RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Consultative Sales &amp;amp; Revenue Leadership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;multilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Own and grow a significant individual revenue pipeline across events, sponsored content, special reports and strategic partnerships.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;multilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;2&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Lead senior-level consultative sales conversations, diagnosing a client&#39;s business, marketing and thought-leadership objectives before recommending solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;multilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;3&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Develop bespoke, multi-platform partnerships rather than relying solely on fixed sponsorship packages or rate-card selling.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
