&lt;p&gt;As the Forward Deployed Engineering Manager, you will lead the team that puts Auterion&#39;s robotic systems to work with customers in the field. We build complete systems: vehicles, sensors, onboard compute, radio links, autonomy software, and ground control. Your job is to understand how all of it fits together and to make it work in real missions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead your team through the entire customer engagement, from discovery and integration to field trials and handover. You are not a hardware specialist. You are a systems engineer who can trace a problem across every layer of the system, lead people well, and earn the trust of demanding customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Mentorship:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead and grow a cross-functional team of Forward Deployed Engineers covering systems integration and software. Hire, coach, and develop your engineers. Build a culture of ownership and proactive problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accountability:&lt;/strong&gt; Keep the bar high for yourself and your team. Work directly with stakeholders across the company. You will have a close relationship with the CTO, CEO, VP of Engineering, and the engineering directors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Deployment Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt; Own technical delivery of customer deployments in demanding, non-standard environments. This covers system configuration, connectivity, mission readiness, and operation under environmental constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the technical lead for high-stakes customer integrations. Ensure the full system works end to end: vehicle, payloads, onboard compute, communication links, autonomy software, and ground control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Troubleshooting:&lt;/strong&gt; Diagnose failures across hardware, firmware, software, and communications. Use logs, telemetry, and structured debugging to find root causes fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary technical contact for defense and enterprise customers. Translate operational requirements into deployment plans that account for system performance, link quality, power, and mission constraints. Run technical meetings, demos, and field days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feedback Loop &amp;amp; Release Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Product and R&amp;amp;D to feed field results and real-world edge cases back into the product. Coordinate with R&amp;amp;D on platform releases so customer deployments stay current and stable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; 7+ years in technical roles in robotics, drones, autonomous vehicles, or comparable complex embedded systems. You understand the full system end to end and how a change in one subsystem affects the others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 3+ years managing a technical, customer-facing team (Field Engineers, Forward Deployed Engineers, Solutions Architects, or similar). You have dealt with underperformance and built team culture deliberately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable working in Linux. You write Python, read C++, and use Git. You debug from logs and telemetry, not only at the bench.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; You understand hardware at integration level: power, sensors, interfaces, and RF basics. You do not need to be a hardware designer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Deployment Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with field-deployed systems where &quot;turning it off and on again&quot; isn&#39;t always an option. Understanding of networking and radio communication is a major plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Crisis Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to troubleshoot critical failures in the field under high pressure and with limited physical access to the hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Presence:&lt;/strong&gt; Composure and credibility in front of demanding customers. You communicate clearly with engineers and decision-makers alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluent English. German is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Authorization:&lt;/strong&gt; Must hold EU citizenship and be eligible to work in the European Union without restriction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4, ArduPilot, or ROS2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in defense or government programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligibility for German security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer at Auterion, you will play a pivotal role in the successful development, integration and deployment of Auterion-powered drone systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will collaborate closely with the production, hardware engineering, and firmware/software teams, as well as operations, ensuring that every platform transitions smoothly from an airframe concept into a fully validated flying robot ready for deployment. You will serve as the primary technical interface for partners, work closely with them to understand their technical requirements, configure and adapt existing solutions, contribute to core software development, and ensure successful implementation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys combining hands-on technical work with customer collaboration and system-level problem solving, bridging the gap between hardware, firmware, and real-world flight performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a highly hands-on environment with evolving system requirements, rapidly iterating across hardware and software integration challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage software releases and perform firmware flashing and configuration using PX4 or adjacent autopilot ecosystems, including sensor calibration, ESC tuning, and system bring-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep avionics and airframe expertise, including autopilot tuning, sensor and payload integration, power systems and airworthiness considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently to troubleshoot integration and flight-readiness issues while collaborating cross-functionally with hardware engineering, firmware/software teams, operations, and QC engineering to escalate complex challenges when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical authority in customer engagements, translating mission requirements into concrete system architectures and demonstrable solutions built on AuterionOS and Skynode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in flight testing activities to validate platform stability, safety, and mission performance, resolving technical issues often directly in the field during customer trials and demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical documentation and continuous improvement of engineering processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed customer and market requirements back into product and engineering teams to influence the roadmap of the Auterion stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Software, Electrical, Mechanical, Aerospace or Robotics Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency in C/C++ and Python: you can read, debug and patch existing code and write small tools and scripts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in Linux environments, including the command line, logs, Docker and basic networking (IP, TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on hardware-software integration: system bring-up, wiring and connectors, and embedded interfaces (UART, CAN, I2C, SPI) at a practical level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured troubleshooting: you can isolate whether a problem is software, hardware, configuration or RF, often under time pressure in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator: you can explain technical issues clearly to customers and operators, and report findings back to engineering in a way they can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel and work on-site with customers, including at test ranges and in field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship (required for security clearance and customer requirements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4 or ArduPilot, MAVLink, QGroundControl or mission planning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UAV flight testing and validation in operational environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with datalinks and radio systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous customer-facing or field engineering role, especially with defense or government customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chainguard is the trusted source for open source. By delivering hardened, secure, and production-ready builds of all the open source software engineers and AI agents rely on, Chainguard helps organizations build faster, stay compliant, and eliminate risk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our customers include Fortune 500 enterprises and global industry leaders, including Anduril, Canva, Fortinet, Hewlett Packard Enterprise, OpenAI, Snap Inc., and Snowflake. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Chainguard is venture-backed by leading investors, including Amplify, IVP, Kleiner Perkins, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Mantis VC, Redpoint Ventures, Sequoia Capital, and Spark Capital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role, in a nutshell:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Renewal Manager, Enterprise at Chainguard, you will play a crucial role in ensuring the retention and long-term success of our largest and most strategic customers. You will own the renewal process for a defined book of high-value accounts, managing complex, multi-year, multi-product renewals from early planning through close while delivering a thoughtful, value-driven customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of Customer Success, Sales, and Ops. You will partner closely with Account Executives and Customer Success Managers on every account: you own the renewal, CSMs own adoption and outcomes, and AEs lead expansion. Your work ensures renewal conversations start early, are grounded in the value customers have realized, and support Chainguard’s broader revenue and retention goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as a trusted partner to customers, guiding renewal conversations with procurement, security leaders, and executives with clarity, empathy, and confidence. Strong business acumen, comfort with complex negotiation, and cross-functional leadership are essential, as each renewal carries significant revenue and requires coordination across many stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Renewal Management: Own the end-to-end renewal process for a portfolio of enterprise customers, starting renewal planning 120+ days out and driving on-time renewals through account strategy, stakeholder engagement, and negotiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Value &amp;amp; Business Case: Partner with CSMs to build renewal business cases grounded in adoption, CVE reduction, and engineering time saved, and present them to economic buyers and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Execution: Structure and negotiate multi-year terms, ramps, co-terms, and pricing changes, and coordinate with Finance, Legal, customer Procurement, and Deal Desk to ensure accurate and timely contract execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account Team Partnership: Work with AEs to align renewals with expansion opportunities, so renewal and growth motions move together rather than compete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecasting &amp;amp; CRM Hygiene: Maintain accurate renewal data in CRM, including forecasts, risks, and renewal status, to provide clear visibility and predictable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk &amp;amp; Retention Strategy: Identify renewal risks early, including budget pressure, adoption gaps, stakeholder changes, and competitive threats, and lead cross-functional plans to mitigate churn and protect gross retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process &amp;amp; Playbooks: Develop and refine enterprise renewal playbooks, including executive engagement and procurement navigation, to increase efficiency and improve on-time renewal rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Mentorship: Serve as the escalation point for the most complex renewals, mentor other Renewal Managers, and help shape how the function scales across segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in B2B SaaS in renewals, account management, or sales, with direct ownership of six-figure customer contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of renewing large, multi-year enterprise agreements at or above value, including through competitive displacement attempts and budget pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to drive complex renewals with predictability and deliver against gross retention targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating multi-year agreements, pricing, and contract terms with enterprise procurement teams while maintaining strong customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort engaging senior stakeholders, including security, engineering, and procurement leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple complex renewal cycles simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort generating quotes, preparing order forms, and maintaining CRM hygiene, ideally in Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High emotional intelligence, strong communication skills, and a proactive, problem-solving mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate with full autonomy in a fast-paced, evolving environment and lead the build-out of new processes where needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strongly Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large enterprises in regulated industries such as financial services or healthcare&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth or early-stage startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with security, DevSecOps, or developer-focused products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for technology and cybersecurity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Range:&lt;/strong&gt; Up to 144,286 GBP 70/30 OTE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;If your experience is close, but doesn’t fulfill all requirements,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;please apply&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; Chainguard is on a mission to build the best team. To achieve our goal, we are focused on hiring Chainguardians with unique backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We live and breathe our company values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are customer obsessed — We focus on delivering solutions to our customers that create value and make their lives better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have a bias for intentional action — We prioritize, plan, try things, and fail fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We don&#39;t take ourselves too seriously (but we do serious work) — We are solving an important problem which takes focus, but we also like to enjoy the journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We trust each other and assume good intentions — We&#39;re transparent with decisions to empower team members to make well informed decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A few of the benefits we offer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible &amp;amp; Remote-First Culture:&lt;/strong&gt; Work remotely with team meetup opportunities, bi-annual destination summits, and a monthly stipend for coworking spaces, phone and internet costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Approach to Equity:&lt;/strong&gt; Receive stock options upon hire and promotion. Plus, you can participate in secondary offerings and have 10 years to exercise your options (yes, you read that correctly: 10 years!).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;100% Covered Health Insurance:&lt;/strong&gt; We cover 100% of your health, vision and dental insurance premiums for you and your dependents. Nothing comes out of your paycheck.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;∞ Flexible Time Off:&lt;/strong&gt; Take the time you need – to do our best work, we need to recharge and reset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;18 Weeks Paid Parental Leave:&lt;/strong&gt; We offer 18 weeks for birthing parents and 12 weeks for non-birthing parents, with the option to use it all at once or throughout your child&#39;s first year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If your experience is close but doesn&#39;t fulfill all requirements, please apply. We&#39;re building the best team in technology and are focused on hiring &quot;Chainguardians&quot; with unique backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chainguard is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you acknowledge that Chainguard will process your personal data in accordance with &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chainguard.dev/legal/candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Chainguard&#39;s Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;©2026 Chainguard. All Rights Reserved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Account Director (Perm, UK, Remote)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Nearform&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nearform is an independent team of data and AI experts, engineers, and designers who build intelligent digital solutions and capabilities at pace. We create AI‑enabled solutions that enhance digital experiences, empower developers, and deliver measurable results. In these ways, we partner with ambitious enterprises to deliver enduring impact. Our deep expertise in solving complex digital problems, along with our collaborative, people‑first approach, enables enterprises to build breakthrough products and modernise legacy systems by unleashing the power of AI. Today, our team of 500 experts in 20+ countries is trusted by leading enterprises including Lululemon, Puma, Sun Life, Starbucks, Travelex, Virgin Media O2, and Walmart&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nearform has worked with this Client for over a decade. They are one of our most strategically important clients — a Client that we both &lt;strong&gt;sell to&lt;/strong&gt; (as a direct client) and &lt;strong&gt;sell with&lt;/strong&gt; (as a partner taking joint propositions to their end-clients).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a strategic account director to own the commercial growth of this account. This is a senior, hands-on role: equal parts business developer, marketer, account strategist, and trusted operator inside one of Nearform&#39;s most important relationships. You will be the commercial centre of gravity for everything Nearform does with this Client.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the executive relationship. &lt;/strong&gt;Build and maintain a network of senior sponsors across the Client’s consulting and technology leadership teams, creating new advocates for Nearform and deepening executive engagement over time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the business development plan.&lt;/strong&gt; Build, maintain, and execute a multi-year account plan with clear targets, named opportunities, and a credible path to growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Win new business, across both sides of the relationship.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead pursuit of new opportunities — directly into this Client and jointly into their end-clients — from origination through to close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring commercial framing to technical pursuits.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Nearform&#39;s Technical Directors and Solutions leaders to translate strong technical propositions into compelling commercial cases that win.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage marketing for the account.&lt;/strong&gt; Own how Nearform shows up in and around this Client — joint content, co-branded propositions, events, case studies, and the steady drumbeat of presence that keeps us front of mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define and align the account management model.&lt;/strong&gt; Agree with the Client (and internally) how the relationship is governed — who meets whom, on what cadence, with what outcomes — and keep that model healthy as the account scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a commercial face of the relationship.&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain senior stakeholder relationships across this account, and act as the internal owner of the commercial health at Nearform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forecast, report, and run the rhythm.&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain accurate pipeline, forecast confidently, and run the operational cadence (QBRs, pipeline reviews, account standups) that keeps the account predictable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work with local GTM teams &lt;/strong&gt;where appropriate so we are bringing local intimacy with global consistency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial track record&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience growing a strategic enterprise account, ideally one that combines direct selling and partner/channel motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of winning new business in a services or technology environment — not just managing existing revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable owning a number and forecasting against it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consulting and Partner fluency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has worked with, in, or alongside consulting firms — understands how they sell, how they buy, and how to be useful to them in front of their clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knows how to navigate a &quot;sell-to and sell-with&quot; relationship without confusing the two&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knows how to elevate the partnership-building dimension to develop and execute joint GTM strategies with the client by identifying repeatable plays, solution offerings and routes to market that creates growth for both organisations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI and technology background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of modern technology delivery — software engineering, cloud, data, and (especially) applied AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credible in technical conversations: doesn&#39;t need to architect the solution, but can shape, qualify, and commercially frame it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversant in the AI landscape as it applies to enterprise — agents, AI-native engineering, the difference between hype and production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operator instincts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plans the work and works the plan — strong account-planning discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident running marketing for an account: brief, prioritise, and partner well with central Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds trust quickly with senior stakeholders, internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable holding the commercial line in a room of technical specialists, and the technical line in a room of commercial buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships in the management consulting ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up or refining an account management operating model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background that includes time in a delivery or technical role earlier in career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibility so they can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data, wherever it lives, and move at the speed of their ambitions. Customers, including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce, rely on Grafana Labs. We are a 100% remote company with team members across 40+ countries, backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://grafana.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;grafana.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and follow us on &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/grafana-labs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/grafana&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote opportunity and we would be interested in applications from the UK, Ireland, Sweden, Spain and Germany.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is building a native experimentation platform: a Grafana app that lets teams define A/B tests, connect them to feature flags and product telemetry, and get trustworthy, statistically sound answers about what their changes actually did.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It started as a hackathon project and is now used by Grafana engineering and product teams in our internal environment to run real experiments. The next step is to make it a first-class product: one we rely on every day internally and, over time, one we offer to Grafana Cloud customers alongside Frontend Observability, Session Replay and our other user-experience capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the &lt;strong&gt;Product Analytics team&lt;/strong&gt;, a group of highly technical product analysts who help teams across Grafana understand how our products are used and run experiments on them. As the team&#39;s dedicated software engineer, you&#39;ll own the engineering of the experimentation app and have a lot of influence over where it goes. You&#39;ll partner closely with data scientists on the statistics, data engineers on event pipelines and the data warehouse, software engineers across Grafana on feature flags, Frontend Observability and the App Platform, and product stakeholders who rely on experiment results to make decisions. This is a hands-on engineering role that ships production code. It is not an analyst role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the product:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The experimentation app is built on the Grafana App Platform:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend:&lt;/strong&gt; a TypeScript and React app plugin using @grafana/ui, plus a custom datasource plugin that powers experiment statistics panels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend:&lt;/strong&gt; Go, built with the Grafana App SDK. Experiments are Kubernetes-style custom resources defined in CUE, with an operator, admission webhooks, and support for declarative, GitOps-style management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feature flags:&lt;/strong&gt; integration with &lt;strong&gt;OpenFeature&lt;/strong&gt; and the &lt;strong&gt;OpenFeature Remote Evaluation Protocol (OFREP)&lt;/strong&gt;, Grafana&#39;s multi-tenant feature toggle service, and an embedded GO Feature Flag evaluator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statistics engine:&lt;/strong&gt; a Bayesian analysis engine (TypeScript, with a Go port) that produces a direction-aware verdict per metric, probability to be best, credible intervals, expected loss and sample-size recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data:&lt;/strong&gt; experiment exposure and outcome events flow from product instrumentation through RudderStack into BigQuery, or from Grafana Faro into Loki, and are queried live through Grafana datasources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI:&lt;/strong&gt; experiment authoring assisted by &lt;strong&gt;Grafana Assistant&lt;/strong&gt;, which discovers relevant data and drafts the experiment configuration for a human to review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evolve the experimentation app from internal tool to product.&lt;/strong&gt; Full ownership of features end to end across the React frontend and Go backend, from problem framing and design through rollout, measurement and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the experimentation experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Develop intuitive workflows for defining hypotheses, configuring experiments and metrics, managing their lifecycle, and exploring results. Make these experiences useful for product managers and analysts as well as engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make instrumentation easier to adopt and trust&lt;/strong&gt;. Evolve the experimentation SDK and its OpenFeature and Faro integrations. Help teams connect variant assignment, actual exposure, and outcome events with consistent identity and event contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connect experiments to the rest of Grafana’s user-experience stack.&lt;/strong&gt; Integrate with Grafana Faro and Frontend Observability so flag exposures and outcomes are captured automatically, and link experiment results to Session Replay and critical user journeys so teams can see &lt;em&gt;why&lt;/em&gt; a variant won, not only &lt;em&gt;that&lt;/em&gt; it won.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Harden the statistics and analysis path.&lt;/strong&gt; Work with our data analysts to extend the statistics engine, and make analysis scalable, cost-aware and correct. Examples include moving computation server-side, scheduled analysis, alerting on experiment health, and guardrails against misleading results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use AI where it genuinely helps.&lt;/strong&gt; Extend the Grafana Assistant integration for authoring, explaining and reporting on experiments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the engineering bar.&lt;/strong&gt; Mentor teammates, including analysts who contribute code, through code review, pairing and design docs. Write the architecture decision records (ADRs), docs and demos that help other teams adopt experimentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own what you ship.&lt;/strong&gt; Take part in on-call for the services you build, and support the internal teams that run experiments on them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest heavily in developer productivity. You can use modern AI coding assistants as part of your daily workflow (your choice of tools, within security guidelines), backed by a company-funded usage budget so you can iterate quickly without unnecessary friction. We encourage pragmatic AI-assisted development: faster prototyping, test generation, refactors, documentation, and incident follow-ups, always with strong code review and quality standards. You’ll also have access to the latest frontier models from OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes you a great fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We highly value people who are intellectually curious, default to transparency, have a strong bias towards action, and are kind and enjoy working as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong full-stack engineering experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve built and operated production web applications with TypeScript and React, and backend services in Go (or a similar language, with willingness to work in Go). You value maintainability, automated testing and secure development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience building an in-house platform or integrating existing experimentation and A/B testing platform &lt;/strong&gt;(for example Statsig, Eppo, GrowthBook, Optimizely, LaunchDarkly experiments, or an in-house platform).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product and data intuition.&lt;/strong&gt; You care whether what you shipped actually moved the needle, and you’re comfortable working with event data, SQL and data warehouses such as BigQuery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve delivered complex projects with minimal supervision, broken them into short feedback loops (analyze, design, ship an MVP, learn, iterate), and helped teammates work more effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational responsibility.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve been on call, supported software in production, and know how to make systems observable and debuggable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pragmatic AI usage.&lt;/strong&gt; You use AI coding tools thoughtfully, validate their output, and share practices that improve the team’s speed &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear communication.&lt;/strong&gt; You can explain technical and statistical tradeoffs to engineers, analysts and product managers in a fully remote, asynchronous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with feature flags and OpenFeature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working understanding of experiment statistics: Bayesian or frequentist testing, sample sizing, variance reduction, and common pitfalls such as peeking and sample ratio mismatch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kubernetes concepts: custom resources, operators, admission webhooks, GitOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building Grafana plugins or apps, or with the Grafana App SDK or Scenes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with frontend observability and product analytics tooling, such as Grafana Faro, RUM, session replay, RudderStack or Segment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open source contribution or maintainership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a user of Grafana, Prometheus, Loki or Tempo, whether at work or on a homelab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Rewards:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the UK, the base compensation range for this role is £94&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;,000 - £118,000&lt;/span&gt;. Actual compensation may vary based on level, experience, and skillset as assessed throughout the interview process. All of our roles include Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), giving every team member ownership in Grafana Labs&#39; success. We believe in shared outcomes—RSUs help us stay aligned and invested as we scale globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;*Compensation ranges are country specific. If you are applying for this role from a different location than listed above, your recruiter will discuss your specific market’s defined pay range &amp;amp; benefits at the beginning of the process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Thrive at Grafana Labs:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;100% Remote, Global Culture -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;As a remote-only company, we bring together talent from around the world, united by a culture of collaboration and shared purpose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling Organization&lt;/strong&gt; – Tackle meaningful work in a high-growth, ever-evolving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transparent Communication&lt;/strong&gt; – Expect open decision-making and regular company-wide updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation-Driven&lt;/strong&gt; – Autonomy and support to ship great work and try new things.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Source Roots&lt;/strong&gt; – Built on community-driven values that shape how we work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empowered Teams&lt;/strong&gt; – High trust, low ego culture that values outcomes over optics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Career Growth Pathways&lt;/strong&gt; – Defined opportunities to grow and develop your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Approachable Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; – Transparent execs who are involved, visible, and human.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Passionate People&lt;/strong&gt; – Join a team of smart, supportive folks who care deeply about what they do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Person onboarding &lt;/strong&gt;- We want you to thrive from day 1 with your fellow new ‘Grafanistas’ to learn all about what we do and how we do it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Balance is Key&lt;/strong&gt; - We operate a global annual leave policy of 30 days per annum. 3 days of your annual leave entitlement are reserved for Grafana Shutdown Days to allow the team to really disconnect. &lt;em&gt;*We will comply with local legislation where applicable.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Grafana Labs is an equal opportunities employer. We welcome applications from everyone regardless of race, colour, nationality, origin, caste, sex, gender reassignment identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, religion or belief, disability, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, maternity, marital, family or carer status, or any other characteristic which is protected by local law. We believe that equality and diversity build a strong organisation, and we work hard to ensure that is the foundation of our organisation as we grow.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Grafana Labs may utilize AI tools in its recruitment process to assist in matching information provided in CVs to job postings. The recruitment team will continue to review inbound CVs manually to identify alignment with current openings.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
